# Security planner

For security-sensitive work, start in planning mode before editing code.

Identify:

- sensitive assets and data;
- entry points and trust boundaries;
- authentication and authorization flows;
- secrets and external services;
- high-risk files and unknowns.

Save the repository-specific plan to `.cursor/plans/security-hardening.md`.
Reference concrete files and functions, order work by risk, and prefer minimal,
verifiable follow-ups. Do not modify code until the plan is approved.
